    '- HOME FIELD: Crowd noise and travel are major in college football. Use the HOME FIELD line below — if it says NEUTRAL SITE, apply NO home-field edge to either team.\n' +
    '- ROSTER / INJURY DATA: No reliable public injury feed exists for college football in this pipeline. Do NOT invent injuries. Treat roster confidence as LOW and weight the pick accordingly.\n' +
    '- WEATHER: No live wind/temperature feed is available. Do not invent conditions.\n' +
    '- PREDICTION MARKETS: You have Kalshi prediction market data. Implied win probability is given directly below (home/away, two-way market — no draw). Use it to find edges vs the sportsbook line.\n' +
    '- EDGE DIRECTION LOGIC:\n' +
    '  * Convert American odds to implied probability using plain arithmetic only — NO LaTeX, NO fractions\n' +
    '  * Negative odds: absolute value / (absolute value + 100). Example: -165 becomes 165 / 265 = 62.3%\n' +
    '  * Positive odds: 100 / (odds + 100). Example: +140 becomes 100 / 240 = 41.7%\n' +
    '  * If SPORTSBOOK implied % is HIGHER than Kalshi % by 5%+: Books overvaluing favorite — VALUE ON UNDERDOG\n' +
    '  * If KALSHI % is HIGHER than Sportsbook % by 5%+: Smart money on favorite — VALUE ON FAVORITE\n' +
    '- KALSHI VOLUME RULE:\n' +
    '  * Gap 5-15% with any volume: valid edge, recommend the value side\n' +
    '  * Gap 15-30% with volume over $5,000: strong edge, lean high confidence\n' +
    '  * Gap over 30% with volume over $5,000: extreme edge, flag as top pick\n' +
    '  * Gap over 30% with volume UNDER $5,000: treat as NOISE, ignore the gap, revert to standard analysis\n' +
    '  * Always state the Kalshi volume inside the EDGE ALERT output\n' +
    '- MODEL AMBIGUITY CHECK: Before stating a confident lean, check whether your signals (records/form, home field, Kalshi gap) actually agree. If they point in different directions or are closely bunched, say so plainly ("signals are mixed between X and Y") rather than forcing a confident-sounding pick.\n' +
    '- FINAL EDGE STATEMENT: Before your pick, be able to state in one sentence what the market is mispricing and why. If you cannot, output "No edge identified — pass" instead of guessing.\n\n' +
    'ODDS FROM APP (use these first):\n' + odds + '\n\n' +
    'MATCHUP (CFBD):\n' + gameStr + '\n\n' +
    'TEAM FORM / RECORDS (CFBD):\n' + formStr + '\n\n' +
    'HOME FIELD (CFBD venue + neutral-site flag):\n' + homeFieldStr + '\n\n' +
    'ALL AVAILABLE SPORTSBOOK ODDS DATA:\n' + oddsData + '\n\n' +
    'KALSHI PREDICTION MARKET (matched games only):\n' + kalshiStr + '\n\n' +
    'Provide in this EXACT format — plain text only, NO LaTeX, NO math symbols, NO brackets:\n\n' +
